+//! The feos kernel interface as relibc uses it: call numbers, structures and the
+//! constants that aren't already relibc's (feos's error numbers and file, memory and
+//! signal constants are Linux's, the values relibc's headers already have).
+//!
+//! This is the one place the feos platform keeps them. It's written from
+//! `docs/feos-abi-v2.md` (sections 3 to 7) and has no dependencies, so a host test
+//! (`ports/test/abi-check` in the feos tree) can include it and compare it with the
+//! kernel's own `feos-abi` crate.
